  "body": "### Describe the feature you'd like to request\n\nReference to bug report #5538\n\nFeature request to add support for Unraid storage pools, current GraphQL query only queries the primary array for Unraid.\n\n### Additional information\n\nLooking at the code and running my own GraphQL queries, it looks like Homarr's Unraid integration only supports querying the Unraid primary array (traditional Unraid setup), but does not query pools.\n\nHomarr does not have a full enough query to fetch or process data in a pool-only setup, it would need be updated to query extra fields under the array root field, including (most importantly) caches.\n\nThe caches field is for querying a storage pool that is not the primary array (or boot, or parity)\n\nSomething like this should be merged into the integration code, both to support setups where both the primary array is used as well as pools, or for pool-only setups:\n\n`query { array { caches { id name device size status temp fsSize fsFree fsUsed type isSpinning } } }`\n\nWorth noting that only the first disk in the pool actually reports the size, the others don't, so disks returning \"null\" under fsSize, fsFree, fsUsed should simply be ignored.",
